1. The plain skin, air as a spring: the first three round modes (frequency over the vacuum's)
   B = 0.5: closed form 1.088989, 1.003522, 1.000571; exact matching differs by at most 2.8e-15; finite differences by at most 7.6e-07
   B = 1: closed form 1.169457, 1.007338, 1.001165; exact matching differs by at most 2.2e-16; finite differences by at most 7.6e-07
   B = 2: closed form 1.310399, 1.015959, 1.002424; exact matching differs by at most 7.8e-16; finite differences by at most 7.5e-07
2. The 1954 disc (9.77 times over 0.4) with air as a spring: exact matching against finite differences on 40 rings (the disc's edge is on a ring's edge)
   B = 0: exact 1.006457, 3.071778, 4.851447; finite differences differ by at most 1.0e-06
   B = 1e-06: exact 1.006457, 3.071778, 4.851447; finite differences differ by at most 1.1e-06
   B = 0.5: exact 1.075174, 3.097400, 4.908441; finite differences differ by at most 1.1e-06
   B = 1: exact 1.133759, 3.121242, 4.964400; finite differences differ by at most 1.1e-06
   B = 2: exact 1.228585, 3.163958, 5.071610; finite differences differ by at most 1.2e-06
3. Derivatives with air (B = 1): each miss with respect to the load of rings 3, 9 and 20, against a difference quotient
   largest difference 1.4e-08 with a step of 0.01 (the derivatives themselves are up to 6.0e-03; with smaller steps the quotient is noisier, 1.5e-05 at a step of 1e-05, because the eigenvalues are good to about 1e-9)
4. The tube with a shallow cavity is the spring: the 1954 disc, B = 1, lowest mode
   X = 0.0001: tube 1.133759, spring 1.133759
   X = 0.1: tube 1.133293, spring 1.133759
   X = 0.3: tube 1.129546, spring 1.133759
5. The pole-free condition has the same spring roots: the 1954 disc, B = 1
   largest relative difference 1.9e-13
6. Derivatives when the air's strength follows the load (RefSkin, added after the referee's report): each miss with respect to the load of rings 2, 8, 15 and 21, against a difference quotient with a step of 0.01
   all nine, the lowest as the note: largest difference 1.2e-08 (the derivatives are up to 6.2e-03)
   the lowest aimed at 1.10 and seven overtones: largest difference 2.2e-08 (the derivatives are up to 7.5e-03)
